<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Glad</h1><p class="st-meta">890 CE – 934 CE (approx.) · capital Keve</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Duchy in the Banat described in the Gesta Hungarorum as resisting the conquering Hungarians around 900; its existence is debated.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The main source is the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gesta-hungarorum">Gesta Hungarorum</a>, written by an anonymous notary around 1200. It says <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glad">Glad</a>, who came from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vidin">Vidin</a>, ruled the land between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mures-river">Mureș</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tisza">Tisza</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cumans">Cumans</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgarians">Bulgarians</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vlachs">Vlachs</a>, from the fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kovin">Keve</a> (Kovin).</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Nothing is known of its government beyond the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gesta-hungarorum">Gesta</a>, which claims <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glad">Glad</a> fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magyars">Hungarians</a> with Cuman, Bulgarian and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vlachs">Vlach</a> forces before being defeated and submitting. Historians disagree on whether he was a real ruler, perhaps a Bulgarian governor, or a figure invented from later place-names.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gesta-hungarorum">Gesta</a> says the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magyars">Hungarians</a> took his lands, which then passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-hungary">Principality of Hungary</a>. The same source makes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahtum">Ahtum</a>, of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-ahtum">Duchy of Ahtum</a>, his descendant.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-glad.jpg" alt="Duchy of Glad" width="320" height="187"><figcaption>Image: GeorgeBasaraba · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Banatul_Timi%C8%99oarei_.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>890 CE – 934 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Keve</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Glad</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/romania">Romania</a>, <a href="/countries/serbia">Serbia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Voivodeship of Glad</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=912&amp;focus=duchy-of-glad" aria-label="Duchy of Glad on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5261 564 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Glad lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5437 760h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5581 820h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5581 820h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Romania. <a href="/atlas?year=912&amp;focus=duchy-of-glad">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

